    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d166">

                <pb facs="0456" n="418" xml:id="pg418"/>

                <head>166. Memorandum From the Ambassador-Designate to Iran (Helms) to President
                        Nixon<anchor n="1" xml:id="d166-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1973-02-22">February 22,
                        1973</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Attached is the analysis, requested in your letter to me,<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d166-f2"/> of the Middle East and our interests there as they relate
                    to the growing importance of Middle East energy resources to the United
                    States.</p>
                <p>I have not, in this paper, dwelled on the complexities of the Arab-Israeli
                    problem, even as they relate to our energy interests in the region, because of
                    my feeling that this issue too often clouds our thinking on other important
                    issues such as importance of the Gulf and the Arabian Peninsula in an energy
                    context.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">Richard Helms</hi></signed><anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d166-f3"/></closer>


                <xi:include href="d166-a1.xml" xpointer="d166-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d166-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d166-f1-content">
                <p>Source: National Archives, Nixon Presidential Materials, White House Special
                    Files, President’s Office Files, Box 20, President’s Handwriting, Feb 16–28,
                    1973. Top Secret. A notation on the memorandum indicates that the President saw
                    it. A handwritten notation from Nixon reads, “To E &amp; DiBona—for <hi
                        rendition="#italic">private</hi> info only—not for general circulation.” The
                    attached paper is scheduled to be published in full in <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Foreign Relations</hi>, 1969–1976, volume E–9, Documents on Middle East
                    Region; Arabian Peninsula; North Africa, 1973–1976.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d166-f2" n="2" xml:id="d166-f2-content">
                <p><ref target="#d149">Document 149</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d166-f3" n="3" xml:id="d166-f3-content">
                <p>Helms signed “Dick” above his typed signature.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
